{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.adjacent_weight_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.adjacent_weight_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MarkovOrientationForced.lean#L67-L73","doc":"Level `N`: the `K = q^{2ρ}` weights of adjacent basis vectors `e_i, e_{i+1}` are\n`q^{N-1-2i}` and `q^{N-3-2i}`; their ratio is `q²` for every `N` and `i`.\n(This is the `K` half of the level-`N` weight-space ratio; the equality of the plain traces\non permuted weight spaces is not formalised here.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.markov_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.markov_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MarkovOrientationForced.lean#L61-L65","doc":"With `a b = 1`, the Markov condition gives `a² = q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.same_condition_both_signs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.same_condition_both_signs","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MarkovOrientationForced.lean#L56-L59","doc":"Both crossing signs impose the same condition on `K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.negative_crossing_markov_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.negative_crossing_markov_iff","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MarkovOrientationForced.lean#L42-L54","doc":"Diagonal entries of `tr₂((1⊗K)Ř⁻¹)` agree iff `a = b q²` — the same condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.positive_crossing_markov_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovOrientationForced.positive_crossing_markov_iff","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/MarkovOrientationForced.lean#L28-L40","doc":"Diagonal entries of `tr₂((1⊗K)Ř)` agree iff `a = b q²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}